<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n54096" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατακάμπτω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>bend down</i>, so as to be concave, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξ ὀρθοῦ κ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ti.</u>
				71c
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς ἓν κύκλῳ</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				36b
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. τὰς στροφάς</span>, 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στροφή</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				1.3
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνακάμπτομαι</span>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mete.</u>
				386a1
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φλὲψ ἐπὶ τὴν ῥάχιν -ομένη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					15.530
				</span></i>
			: pf.
			part.
			
				Pass.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κεκαμμένος</span>
			<i>bending over</i>, cj. in <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				3.18.8
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>cover with a vault</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λίθῳ κατακαμφθέντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					5.3.8
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> metaph.,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. ἐλπίδας</span>
			<i>bend down, overthrow</i> hopes, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				1252
			</span></i> (Burges, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-γναψε</span> codd., anap.):—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be bent</i> (by entreaty), <i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
				1.187
			</span></i>.</div>
